    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0816" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.516/364: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chapin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-21T14:00:00-05:00">May 21, 1935—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. See my telegram 34, May 17, 2 [<hi rendition="#italic">1</hi>] p.m., with
                    respect to the Bank Contract.</p>
                <p>Senate unanimously passed without discussion and without modification bill<anchor
                        n="20" xml:id="d717-f1"/> authorizing Government to sign revised contract
                    for purchase of Banque Nationale.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d717-f1" n="20" xml:id="d717-f1-content">
                <p>The law of sanction, dated May 21, approving the modified bank sale contract is
                    printed in <hi rendition="#italic">Le Moniteur</hi>, May 30, 1935, p. 343; also
                    in Haiti, <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin des Lois et Actes</hi>, 1935, p.
                    197.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
